>> servings: 2

Finely shred the @green cabbage{0.5}. Thinly slice the @lebanese cucumber{1} and @red onion{0.25}. Roughly chop the @salted peanuts{3%tbsp}, @fresh coriander{1%bunch} and @dill{0.5%bunch}. Finely slice the @chives{0.5%bunch}. Trim the fat from the @chicken breast{1%large}.

Bring a medium pot of water to the boil. Add the @bay leaf{1}, a pinch of salt, and the juice of @lemon{0.5}. Add the chicken, cover with a lid, reduce the heat to low and cook for ~{9%minutes}. Turn off the heat and let the chicken sit in the hot water for ~{5%minutes} to stay juicy.

Remove the chicken, rest for ~{5%minutes}, then shred with your hands or two forks. Drizzle over @crispy chilli oil{1%tbsp} and set aside.

Combine the cabbage, cucumber, red onion, herbs, @white sesame seeds{1%tbsp} and peanuts in a large bowl. Add the juice of @lemon{0.5}, @white wine vinegar{1%tsp}, a pinch of salt and @crispy chilli oil{2%tsp}. Toss well to combine.

Add the shredded chicken and @cooked brown rice{2%cup} to the salad. Toss again until everything is evenly coated. Taste and adjust with more lemon, salt or crispy chilli oil if needed.

Divide between two bowls and finish with dollops of @chilli egg mayo{}.
